NAME
       grpconv - move group passwords into /etc/gshadow

SYNOPSIS
       grpconv
       grpunconv

DESCRIPTION
       grpconv creates or updates /etc/gshadow from /etc/group: any group
       password still kept in /etc/group is moved to /etc/gshadow and replaced
       by an "x" in /etc/group. Entries in /etc/gshadow for groups that no
       longer exist are removed. grpunconv does the opposite and is almost
       never wanted.

       RHEL 9 installs with shadow group files already in use, so grpconv is
       only needed after someone has edited the files by hand and broken the
       pairing. pwconv does the same job for /etc/passwd and /etc/shadow.

EXAMPLES
              # grpconv
              # grpck -r

FILES
       /etc/group, /etc/gshadow

SEE ALSO
       grpck(8), pwconv(8), group(5), gshadow(5)
